1
00:00:00,550 --> 00:00:04,213
If you find a photo of yourself
you never took... keep it.

2
00:00:04,263 --> 00:00:07,343
Do not throw it away.
Do not show it to anyone.

3
00:00:07,445 --> 00:00:09,960
And do not try to
remember when it happened.

4
00:00:10,032 --> 00:00:11,555
You already looked at it twice.

5
00:00:11,605 --> 00:00:14,030
You told yourself it was
someone who looks like you.

6
00:00:14,081 --> 00:00:17,016
It is not. You have your own ears.

7
00:00:17,073 --> 00:00:19,010
A photograph needs a photographer.

8
00:00:19,060 --> 00:00:20,565
You would remember a flash.

9
00:00:20,658 --> 00:00:24,549
So someone stood close enough to
take it, and you did not notice.

10
00:00:24,599 --> 00:00:26,819
Management has prepared a short briefing.

11
00:00:26,869 --> 00:00:29,804
It will last as long as the
photograph stays in your hand.

12
00:00:30,454 --> 00:00:31,479
Check the corner.

13
00:00:32,429 --> 00:00:35,814
A photographer usually
stands a few metres away.

14
00:00:35,886 --> 00:00:38,016
This one stood forty metres away.

15
00:00:38,336 --> 00:00:41,061
That is a great deal of faith
to place in a zoom lens.

16
00:00:41,511 --> 00:00:45,926
Four things will happen.
Each one brings the photographer closer.

17
00:00:45,976 --> 00:00:49,116
After that, we need to talk
about when it was taken.

18
00:00:50,166 --> 00:00:53,120
One. It was taken from far away.

19
00:00:53,208 --> 00:00:55,894
Look at the edges.
The frame is slightly crooked.

20
00:00:55,944 --> 00:00:59,084
Like someone was trying
very hard not to be seen.

21
00:00:59,134 --> 00:01:00,914
Now look at what you are doing in it.

22
00:01:01,164 --> 00:01:06,646
Nothing. A bus stop. A coffee.
Staring at nothing in particular.

23
00:01:06,696 --> 00:01:10,735
Not posing. Not performing.
Not holding your stomach in.

24
00:01:10,785 --> 00:01:14,955
You have not looked like that
in a photograph for years.

25
00:01:15,355 --> 00:01:17,340
Here is the only rule that matters today.

26
00:01:17,540 --> 00:01:20,635
Do not ask who took it. Ask when.

27
00:01:20,691 --> 00:01:23,421
Asking who sends you
looking for a stranger.

28
00:01:23,519 --> 00:01:26,418
And strangers are a
poor use of an evening.

29
00:01:26,468 --> 00:01:29,383
You have been checking faces on
the street since you found it.

30
00:01:29,683 --> 00:01:33,723
It was not them. Management counted.
You checked forty one.

31
00:01:35,023 --> 00:01:38,673
Two. It will not stay the same.

32
00:01:38,873 --> 00:01:42,038
Put it down. Look away. Look back.

33
00:01:42,488 --> 00:01:43,918
There is a scarf now.

34
00:01:44,039 --> 00:01:47,124
You do not own a scarf like that. Not yet.

35
00:01:47,624 --> 00:01:51,674
And the photograph has started
turning up in other places.

36
00:01:51,752 --> 00:01:55,679
In your phone, between two
pictures you do remember.

37
00:01:55,729 --> 00:01:59,164
On a shelf, behind
someone on a video call.

38
00:01:59,258 --> 00:02:03,378
In a photo booth strip, between
three strangers pulling faces.

39
00:02:03,469 --> 00:02:06,594
In the window of a shop
you only ever walk past.

40
00:02:06,894 --> 00:02:09,329
Do not go looking for the others.

41
00:02:09,529 --> 00:02:13,509
In every one of them,
you look tidy and unbothered.

42
00:02:13,591 --> 00:02:16,741
That is not a keepsake. That is a trailer.

43
00:02:18,041 --> 00:02:21,261
Three. You are not alone in it.

44
00:02:21,366 --> 00:02:24,656
At the edge of the frame,
there is a hand on your shoulder.

45
00:02:24,706 --> 00:02:27,646
Someone is standing
beside you, cropped out.

46
00:02:27,742 --> 00:02:31,002
Whoever it is, you are laughing
at something they said.

47
00:02:31,302 --> 00:02:33,416
Look at that laugh. The real one.

48
00:02:33,466 --> 00:02:36,346
The one that escapes
before you can manage it.

49
00:02:36,455 --> 00:02:38,970
Nobody gets that face on request.

50
00:02:39,270 --> 00:02:41,685
People photograph you saying cheese.

51
00:02:41,742 --> 00:02:45,387
Cheese is a performance.
This is not cheese.

52
00:02:45,687 --> 00:02:48,952
Do not ask whose hand it is. Ask when.

53
00:02:49,252 --> 00:02:50,617
Now turn it over.

54
00:02:50,767 --> 00:02:52,867
(Keep it.)

55
00:02:52,917 --> 00:02:54,551
It is in your handwriting.

56
00:02:54,601 --> 00:02:58,006
Do not compare it with your own.
Do not hold it to the light.

57
00:02:58,326 --> 00:02:59,542
You have done both.

58
00:02:59,592 --> 00:03:02,667
Management has compared it. It is yours.

59
00:03:03,967 --> 00:03:06,984
Four. It will be warm.

60
00:03:07,034 --> 00:03:10,890
Warm like it just came out of
the camera. Warm like a hand.

61
00:03:10,940 --> 00:03:14,020
Each time you look,
the laugh is a little wider.

62
00:03:14,270 --> 00:03:18,010
The photograph is not finished.
Neither is the moment.

63
00:03:18,105 --> 00:03:21,705
Management finds this the most
unsettling item on the list.

64
00:03:22,105 --> 00:03:23,810
Do not put it in a drawer.

65
00:03:23,929 --> 00:03:27,063
A drawer is where you keep
things you are afraid of.

66
00:03:27,113 --> 00:03:28,423
Keep it where you can see it.

67
00:03:28,532 --> 00:03:32,237
It is the only photograph you
own that is still happening.

68
00:03:34,237 --> 00:03:36,392
Now. When it was taken.

69
00:03:36,842 --> 00:03:37,882
Check the corner.

70
00:03:39,932 --> 00:03:42,252
You asked how close. Wrong unit.

71
00:03:42,552 --> 00:03:46,002
It was never far away in space.
It was far away in time.

72
00:03:46,302 --> 00:03:50,067
Nobody followed you.
The photograph has not happened yet.

73
00:03:50,267 --> 00:03:52,957
You are looking at a Tuesday
that has not arrived.

74
00:03:53,457 --> 00:03:56,864
The scarf.
The hand on your shoulder. The laugh.

75
00:03:56,914 --> 00:03:58,304
All of it is on its way.

76
00:03:58,704 --> 00:04:02,221
You have been bracing for next
year like a weather report.

77
00:04:02,271 --> 00:04:05,371
And someone sent you the
one good photograph from it.

78
00:04:05,521 --> 00:04:07,596
In advance. With a note.

79
00:04:07,896 --> 00:04:12,071
It is a generous thing to send.
It is a poor way to deliver it.

80
00:04:12,321 --> 00:04:14,416
And you spent the evening
checking strangers.

81
00:04:15,816 --> 00:04:17,876
So here is how you keep it.

82
00:04:18,076 --> 00:04:19,246
Do nothing about it.

83
00:04:19,546 --> 00:04:22,991
Do not look for the bus stop.
Do not buy the scarf.

84
00:04:23,100 --> 00:04:27,955
Do not try to arrange the laugh.
Moments built on purpose come out stiff.

85
00:04:28,255 --> 00:04:32,820
Go to work. Come home.
Pass the photograph on the way to the kettle.

86
00:04:33,070 --> 00:04:35,085
And live the days in between.

87
00:04:35,385 --> 00:04:39,495
All four hundred and twelve.
The ordinary ones too.

88
00:04:39,561 --> 00:04:41,876
The bad ones are part of the route.

89
00:04:41,965 --> 00:04:44,518
Do not hurry the date. Do not pose.

90
00:04:44,568 --> 00:04:46,728
The number will shrink without your help.

91
00:04:47,328 --> 00:04:48,878
Check the corner.

92
00:04:51,178 --> 00:04:56,213
And then, on an ordinary Tuesday,
someone beside you will say something small.

93
00:04:56,512 --> 00:04:58,558
You will laugh before you can manage it.

94
00:05:00,158 --> 00:05:04,142
Somewhere, a shutter clicks.
Right on time.

95
00:05:05,742 --> 00:05:06,818
One more thing.

96
00:05:06,881 --> 00:05:10,501
Earlier, Management told you
not to show it to anyone.

97
00:05:10,568 --> 00:05:13,168
Management has reviewed that advice.

98
00:05:13,568 --> 00:05:16,383
Frame it. Put it where people can see it.

99
00:05:16,833 --> 00:05:19,546
Management has to correct the record.

100
00:05:19,596 --> 00:05:22,971
Nobody was following you.
Nobody took anything from you.

101
00:05:23,028 --> 00:05:27,158
It was never surveillance.
It was only ever a reminder.

102
00:05:27,458 --> 00:05:30,388
That one day, someone is going
to be glad you were there.

103
00:05:31,088 --> 00:05:32,533
The handwriting was yours.

104
00:05:32,583 --> 00:05:35,903
You will write it about four
hundred and twelve days from now.

105
00:05:36,503 --> 00:05:38,838
Tomorrow, you may find another one.

106
00:05:38,902 --> 00:05:42,507
That is fine. It is only the
good days, arriving early.

107
00:05:42,807 --> 00:05:43,607
Keep them.

108
00:05:44,072 --> 00:05:46,387
Management regrets the misunderstanding.
